{"id": "8e932407-8fc7-4078-8831-71b3e8c72c94", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:28:17.667070", "source": "user", "parent_id": "e770792d-dbf2-43aa-af8d-2d9589698276", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: produ ce a final experiment design (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility) that addresses whether trajectories sampled from the forward simulation model show distributional similarity to ground-truth all-atom MD trajectories on tetrapeptides, evaluated across (a) backbone torsion angles, (b) sidechain torsion angles, and (c) top TICA components. No execution or compute is required; treat tract.md as the primary input and confirm the workspace is empty / non-essential before proposing. Please reply now with: (1) inspection notes on /workspace and any inputs you can read (e.g., tract.md) — quote what is actually present, do not infer contents you cannot see; (2) a concise proposed approach covering: the system (tetrapeptides, all-atom MD ground truth, forward-simulation model), sampling protocol (number of replicas, trajectory length, initial-state distribution, temperature/solvent/force-field assumptions you intend to *fix by design* rather than measure), collective-variable definitions (how you will compute φ/ψ/χ, Ramachandran/free-energy 1D–2D projections, and TICA features/lag/top-k selection strategy), distributional-similarity metrics (e.g., 1D/2D KDE overlap, JS or Wasserstein distances, free-energy RMSE, population flips in TICA metastable states, optionally a multivariate test such as MMD), controls and baselines (e.g., a held-out MD set, a randomized/native-control, and ideally a degraded-model ablation to anchor the metric scale), and feasibility (tools you would assume available, e.g., MDTraj/PyEMMA/Plumed, dependencies you note as required, and a rough computational footprint expressed in design terms, not as a promised run); (3) explicit assumptions and uncertainties you flag — in particular (i) which exact forward-simulation model and which MD dataset/sequence set you intend to scope, (ii) the TICA eigenmode-to-top-k choice rule, (iii) the convergence/diagnostic plan (block analysis, effective sample size, bootstrap CIs on the similarity metrics), and (iv) any stopping rule for declaring distributional similarity. Keep this proposal compact and source-grounded; do not yet produce the full design document. We will lock the approach on the next turn.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Do the sampled trajectories from the forward simulation model exhibit distributional similarity to ground-truth MD trajectories across key collective variables, such as backbone torsions, sidechain torsions, and top TICA components?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_2\", \"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_13\", \"neurips2024/93022/0:setup_14\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
