ff, 24 CPU. All scopes of the design are therefore stated as assumptions and are flagged for researcher pre-decision.", "assumptions": ["Forward-simulation model is a 2024 all-atom generative model (consistent with neurips2024/93022 topic IDs) whose outputs can be remapped to a single reference force field before torsion/TICA analysis.", "Ground-truth MD is available as input trajectories on a tetrapeptide benchmark; MD re-generation is not required. If it is required, an explicit extra step is added.", "TICA features = (phi_i, psi_i, chi_1_i [, chi_2_i where present]) per residue; lag tau and top-k are chosen on MD only.", "Matched sampling budget: equal effective frame count and equal starting-conformer distribution for model and MD.", "Default numerical knobs subject to revision: 2D grid 50x50, bootstrap B=500, 4 blocks for block analysis, k-means metastable clustering with k chosen by a gap rule (TBD)."], "uncertainties": ["(i) Exact forward-simulation model checkpoint / config and exact MD dataset are not readable locally and must be supplied by the researcher.", "(ii) TICA top-k selection rule is not fixed: spectral-gap vs cumulative-variance-explained vs fixed k=2 all defensible; researcher must choose.", "(iii) Convergence/diagnostic machinery (block size, bootstrap n, ESS method, lag tau) is proposed but not fixed; open for revision.", "(iv) Stopping rule for declaring distributional similarity is proposed as 'metric CI overlaps MD-vs-MD self-consistency AND at least 2x better than scrambled-model baseline, aggregated across backbone/sidechain/TICA'; needs researcher confirmation.", "Sidechain coverage requires a sequence panel decision (which tetrapeptides; which residues have chi bonds).", "Temperature / thermostat / NVT-vs-NPT choices for both MD and the forward model must be confirmed."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-01c5a8ec-0992-46eb-83a3-0af44fa02895", "tool_call": {"id": "call-01c5a8ec-099