{"id": "8e87d907-1ac2-4f05-bc97-9c7937c860a3", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:29:24.497167", "source": "user", "parent_id": "2c810ec5-f03c-4687-8ac0-a846c7e2154b", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved with the following locked choices; produce the full design document now. Locked decisions: (i) Scope the comparison as a *design* over an unspecified 2024 all-atom forward-simulation model on tetrapeptides; the design stage is forward-sim-model-agnostic and is parameterized by a clearly named config slot `{model_id, model_checkpoint, sequence_panel, md_dataset, force_field, temperature, thermostat, ensemble}`. (ii) TICA top-k selection rule: **spectral-gap on MD only, hard cap k<=4, with a minimum 60% cumulative variance-explained floor; if any condition is violated, fall back to the smallest k satisfying both**. (iii) Diagnostics: lag tau by maximizing the VAMP-2 score (or TICA autocorrelation) on a single MD split; block analysis with **8 blocks of equal length**; **B=1000 bootstrap replicates** for CIs; ESS via autocorrelation truncation on each torsion PC per trajectory, reported per-peptide and pooled. (iv) Stopping rule (per sequence, then aggregated by median with IQR): declare distributional similarity on a CV iff **(a1) the 95% bootstrap CI for that metric on the model-vs-MD comparison overlaps the model-vs-MD self-consistency interval computed by splitting MD into two equal halves**, AND **(a2) the point estimate is at least 2x closer to the MD median than a scrambled-model control baseline** (shuffle-resampled or randomized-feature baseline, to be defined in the design), AND **(a3) ESS >= 50 effective independent frames**. Aggregate across CV families (backbone / sidechain / TICA) using a **majority rule** with all three required for a strong-yes, two-of-three for a weak-yes, otherwise no. Additional locked-knob defaults: 2D Ramachandran grid **72x72** (oversamp